# Project Goals

What [SET AT SETUP: PROJECT_NAME] is for, and the standing facts every
Controller and Planner should know. A reference, not a gate: directives say
which objective they serve (`Serves: 3`), or `Serves: —` when none fits.
Only the user changes the objectives.

Planning is two layers: this file, and the directives themselves
(`plans/directives/<ID>.md`). **The directive is the plan.** When a body of
work needs a signed, durable scope, the Architect writes a short spec in
`docs/specs/` and directives cite its requirement IDs.

